From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: disable HW ATF

Firmware stops accepting per-station VOW DRR commands after band
stop/start cycles. Every UNI_CMD_VOW STA request on the affected
band is rejected with status 0xC0000001, including a plain
VOW_DRR_CTRL_STA_PAUSE with a zero payload, while band level VOW
configuration is still accepted. Reprogramming the VOW engine on
band start does not recover it; only a full firmware reload does.

Since da2c90d2167d ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: send the STA_REC before the
per-station VoW setup") the rejection no longer blocks association,
but the driver does not log it, the station keeps no airtime weight,
and an MLO link that comes back before the station is authorized
still fails on it. Send no VOW command until the firmware accepts
per-station commands after a band restart.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -2776,6 +2776,11 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_vow_drr_ctrl(struct m
 		.omac_idx = mvif ? mvif->omac_idx : 0,
 	};
 
+	/* HW ATF disabled: after band stop/start cycles the firmware
+	 * rejects every per-station VOW command until it is reloaded
+	 */
+	return 0;
+
 	switch (id) {
 	case VOW_DRR_CTRL_STA_ALL:
 		val |= FIELD_PREP(VOW_DRR_STA_BSS_GRP_MASK,
@@ -2868,6 +2873,9 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_vow_feature_ctrl(stru
 		.bwc_enable_per_grp = cpu_to_le16(0xffff),
 	};
 
+	/* HW ATF disabled, see mt7996_mcu_set_vow_drr_ctrl() */
+	return 0;
+
 	/* apply every field this command configures */
 	apply = VOW_FEATURE_APPLY_REFILL_PERIOD | VOW_FEATURE_BAND1_SEARCH_RULE |
 		VOW_FEATURE_BAND0_SEARCH_RULE | VOW_FEATURE_WATF_EN |
